{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented + pushed as Gerrit change 1301 (commit d2b5ab98b9). Shared _iter_cursor_pages walk + RunawayPaginationError in acli_graph.py (637 LOC, under cap); all three readers rewired with 'except RunawayPaginationError: raise' ahead of their fail-open handlers — ordinary faults keep the documented degrade-open contract (partial map, 410 loud). Held-out suite re-pinned: cabc-7a98 strict-xfail flipped to a plain assertion parametrized over all three readers; added iterator-level oracles (multi-page echo, both terminators, single page, repeated-token raise, transport-fault propagation, non-dict quiet stop), a mid-walk-fault degrade-open test per reader, and a structural no-hand-loops guard. Mutation-checked: disabling the raise fails 4 tests by name. Full reconciler suite 2056 passed (1 known env-dependent test_ref_lock failure, pre-existing). Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785776236910067001,"uuid":"9bf45e1a-6499-4009-8857-f28fc50ed75d"}